<article class="env-remark" id="03JY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03JY">Remark <span data-tag="03JY">68.6.3</span>.</a> Reasonable algebraic spaces are technically easier to work with than very reasonable algebraic spaces. For example, if $X \to Y$ is a quasi-compact étale surjective morphism of algebraic spaces and $X$ is reasonable, then so is $Y$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/03L2" data-tag="03L2">68.17.8</a> but we don't know if this is true for the property “very reasonable”. Below we give another technical property enjoyed by reasonable algebraic spaces. </p>
